{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7ae5c905-a037-494e-9ff0-65818c7f0d82","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a16e0fec5cf295e7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-t7iskpk6/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Manager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic converts reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller to standard camelCase field names, and adds the `resourceKind` structured field across all controller tiers. It delivers the manager-binary portion of the operator reconciliation log standardization strategy: every reconciliation error log in the manager binary becomes queryable by resource name, namespace, and kind without parsing message text.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe manager binary contains five controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus 15 action files across four tiers:\n\n- 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`)\n- 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`)\n- 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`)\n- 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n\nWork items:\n\n1. **Audit**: enumerate all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across all five controller tiers and the 15 action files, using grep/static analysis; produce a tracked call-site checklist that confirms (or corrects) the estimate that ~75% of calls embed resource identity in message strings.\n2. **Convert message-embedded identity**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity and emit it as structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), leaving a clean message string.\n3. **DSCI key migration**: replace the non-standard field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` with the standard `name`/`namespace` convention.\n4. **Add `resourceKind`**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all controllers — service, module, DSC, DSCI, component, and DSC controllers (for component/DSC controllers the kind is implied by the controller name, so this is a cross-controller queryability enhancement performed on the same call sites being converted).\n5. **Cluster-scoped resources**: for cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization), emit `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious namespace value.\n6. **CI lint rule**: author a CI lint/static-analysis rule that flags `log.Error` calls embedding name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields, and verify its coverage over all manager-binary code paths. The rule is co-delivered with this epic's conversion so the surface that converts also enforces.\n7. **Unit tests**: tests parsing test logger output to assert field presence and correctness for service controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and all 15 action files; a test asserting DSCI uses the standard field names.\n8. **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes; identify text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns and coordinate updates with SRE/Support.\n\nField naming follows camelCase (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) per the Staff Engineer / SME input, matching controller-runtime's structured log key conventions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given any manager-binary reconciliation error log that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, the updated call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), measured by the CI lint rule or static analysis flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text across manager-binary paths.\n- All DSCI controller structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), measured by a unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` remain.\n- Every service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error log includes `resourceKind`, measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n- Every action file error log across all 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module) includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n- Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers, measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n- DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`, measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n- Cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` with namespace omitted or empty, measured by a unit test confirming no spurious namespace value.\n- The CI lint rule authored in this epic runs in CI and passes with zero violations over manager-binary code paths.\n- The audit deliverable exists as a tracked checklist covering all `log.Error` call sites in the manager binary, with the observed embedded-identity percentage recorded.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and both formats are ingested by the production log consumer stack without configuration changes; text-based alert rules relying on message-string patterns are identified and update coordination with SRE/Support is recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 — reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace converted to structured KV pairs | P0 | Manager-binary portion: all five controller tiers and 15 action files |\n| HLR-2 — DSCI migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace` | P0 | Full |\n| HLR-3 — service controllers include `resourceKind` | P0 | Full (all 5 service controllers) |\n| HLR-4 — all 15 action files include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` | P0 | Full |\n| HLR-6 — module controller error logs include the three fields across 8 module handlers | P0 | Full |\n| HLR-7 — DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` | P1 | Full, bundled with the P0 conversion: the `resourceKind` addition targets the same `log.Error` call sites in the same files as the P0 structured-conversion work, so it is not independently deferrable — splitting it would force a second pass over the same call sites with no standalone value |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59914,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-865e0e4e9f1fc2aa","agent_id":"a7c2659a9f7c83256","session_id":"baaaf3ac-65f4-4aef-b7ec-53586eccdd51","uuid":"c51259bd-52d5-4d53-863c-67395444421f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:06.161Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
