{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97fdf1e9bfdb8a39","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Structured log field convention guideline and external publication\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: 0\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Structured log field convention guideline and external publication\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic authors and publishes the structured log field convention for rhods-operator reconciliation logging: a contribution guideline that specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`) that motivated the standardization. It also publishes the convention externally for voluntary adoption by other operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per platform policy, which prohibits RHOAI from mandating or managing external operator dependencies.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\tContent outline for the contribution guideline (new documentation topic in the rhods-operator repository's contributor documentation):\n40\t\n41\t1. **Required structured fields**: `name`, `namespace` (P0), and `resourceKind`, with the distinction that `resourceKind` is critical for controllers that do not reconcile a single kind (service controllers, module handlers, cloudmanager controllers) and a queryability enhancement for single-kind component controllers.\n42\t2. **camelCase naming rationale**: alignment with controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions.\n43\t3. **Three-problem diagnosis**: message-embedded resource identity, DSCI non-standard key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and the missing `resourceKind` field — with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n44\t4. **DSCI key migration guide**: release-notes-ready documentation of the migration from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`, including before/after query examples for operators with existing Loki/CloudWatch queries, noting that the transition happens in a single release to avoid long-term inconsistency.\n45\t5. **Cluster-scoped resource handling**: `namespace` omitted or empty for cluster-scoped resources.\n46\t6. **CI enforcement**: how the structured-log lint rule flags non-conforming `log.Error` calls in new controller development.\n47\t\n48\tAdditional deliverables:\n49\t\n50\t- **Decision record on additional fields**: record the product/observability decision on whether the convention includes fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category), or explicitly defers them, with the log-volume trade-off noted.\n51\t- **External publication**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by external operator teams and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator). Adoption remains at those teams' discretion per platform policy overlay 0008 — the deliverable is publication, not adoption.\n52\t- **Technical review**: the guideline's examples and field list are reviewed against the implemented conversion in the manager and cloudmanager binaries so the documented convention matches what was actually built.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The contribution guideline exists in the rhods-operator contributor documentation, specifying the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis, with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n57\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversions: every field name, example call, and claim in the guideline matches the merged implementation.\n58\t- The DSCI key migration section provides before/after query examples suitable for release notes, covering operators with existing Loki/CloudWatch queries on the old field names.\n59\t- The guideline records the decision on additional fields beyond name/namespace/kind (included, deferred, or rejected, with rationale).\n60\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects; voluntary adoption per platform policy is noted in the publication.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n65\t|-----|----------|----------|\n66\t| HLR-8 — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption | P1 | Full |\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4c24c37a819e3d5","agent_id":"a447e31c7c13a529d","session_id":"baaaf3ac-65f4-4aef-b7ec-53586eccdd51","uuid":"76f5654f-9f7d-4ac4-95b7-04f1e0bce98b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:48:35.192Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-97fdf1e9bfdb8a39","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
