aceability matrix present in the summary and per-epic. No priority collapse with independently deferrable features.\n26\t\n27\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n28\tFrontmatter dependencies match the diagram exactly: E003 depends on [E001, E002]; both edges are Rule 11 docs-last edges (valid, and exempt from priority inheritance). E001 ∥ E002 have no edge — correct under Rule 15 (same repo, disjoint binaries/controller sets). No circular dependencies, no invalid edges, no branch files, no konflux-onboarding epics (so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is vacuously satisfied). Critical path length 2 fits the S-size heuristic (1-2). Cross-check of epic content for uncaptured data/artifact dependencies: the one candidate — E002's verification AC being measured by the CI lint rule whose authorship is a work item of E001 — was examined and is the rule-compliant AC-gate shape, not a missing DAG edge: E002's own scope commits it to verifying and extending the rule's coverage over cloudmanager paths itself (shared-surface enforcement division), so the coupling is enforcement content plus merge coordination, both explicitly justified in the DAG Justification and Health Warning 7. Watch note only, no issue.\n29\t\n30\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n31\tAll three epics are ODH Operator team / OpenShift AI Productization — the manager/cloudmanager split is by sub-system (separate binaries, disjoint controller sets), justified in the Triage Decision, not a team-boundary violation. No scope duplication between E001 and E002 (disjoint binaries); E003 is a distinct content deliverable. No work-product type mixing — code (E001/E002) and content authoring (E003) are separate epics. No standalone lint-rule epic (correct shared-surface shape: the enforcement deliverable is divided per surface into the consuming epics). Size: E001 is the one epic at/slightly above the ~2-week guideline (~1-1.5 sprints), but it is a single mechanical conversion applied uniformly over an enumerated surface (5 controller tiers, 15 action files) presented by the strategy as one work item, and Health Warning 1 carries a concrete conditional re-split trigger (audit materially exceeding the 75% estimate, or capacity constraints, with controller-tier seams named) — per the size-classification rules this is a watch note, not a split demand.\n32\t\n33\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n34\tNo Investigation epics — every open question was correctly tested against \"does the answer change which epics exist or what they do\" and failed (audit percentage changes volume, not structure; alert-rule inventory is fix-and-retry identification work; cloudmanager release timing is scheduling; additional-fields decision is recorded content). All three epics are Implementation and produce concrete artifacts (converted call sites, checklist, lint rule, tests, published guideline). All `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are null and no epic lists an Investigation in `dependencies`, so no gating-metadata defects are possible. E003's `implementation_type: docs-authoring` is correct for a contribution-guideline authoring epic.\n35\t\n36\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n37\tAll three epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with `investigation_signals: null` — type-appropriate. All three ai-signals files exist with per-signal rationales that match the frontmatter values. Spot-checks: E001/E002 `change_specificity: 1` justified by exact file inventories and named controllers; `pattern_precedent: 1` justified by the SME-confirmed in-repo structured-log precedent; E003 `pattern_precedent: 0` justified (new guideline, no existing doc to pattern on). E003 `open_questions: 0` was scrutinized for contradiction with its \"unaffected by the answer\" rationale — the value is defensible because the additional-fields decision is a pending PM/Observability input the deliverable must record, unlike E001's unknowns which change volume only; not a rubric contradiction. Calibration check on `architecture_claims`: the strategy asserts component states (5 controller tiers, action-file inventory, cloudmanager binary, shared reconciler); the cited context file `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/rhods-operator.md` exists and covers rhods-operator, and all three epics score `architecture_claims: 1` citing it — the E001 rationale even reconciles the context file's coarser \"three tiers\" phrasing against the SME-corrected five-tier description. No arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n38\t\n39\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n40\tEvery epic has testable ACs with \"measured by\" clauses. Rule-mandated ACs: E003 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC against the implemented conversions; no replacement epics exist (rollback/feature-flag N/A — additive log-field change); no konflux chain (N/A). Soft-AC scan: the before/after log-consumer ingestion ACs are conditions on work the epics themselves build and verify (dev-cluster deploy, triggered errors, comparison), not externally-granted preconditions — valid ACs. E003 correctly keeps COO adoption out of the ACs (publication and tracking-issue filing are the epic's own deliverables; voluntary adoption is noted as such). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references use descriptive names (\"the manager-binary conversion\").\n41\t\n42\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n43\tAll strategy scope is covered: every strategy acceptance criterion has a corresponding epic AC (structured conversion, DSCI migration, service-controller resourceKind, 15 action files, cloudmanager controllers, cluster-scoped handling, documented convention), the NFR backwards-compatibility verification is an AC on both implementation epics, the performance NFR requires no verification (correctly not carried), and all four risks have carried-forward mitigations (lint rule + checklist, log-consumer verification AC, publication + tracking issues, DSCI migration guide with before/after query examples in E003). All four open questions are dispositioned with two becoming concrete ACs (E003 decision record; E001 alert-rule coordination). No conditional branches are needed — no bounded outcome changes epic structure. One minor gap (see issues): E002's backwards-compatibility AC covers the before/after ingestion comparison but omits the text-based alert-rule identification and SRE/Support coordination that the summary's Open Question Disposition states is an acceptance criterion on E002 as well — E001 carries it, E002 does not.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adedd3562747cce6","agent_id":"a986b9c2efa209945","session_id":"baaaf3ac-65f4-4aef-b7ec-53586eccdd51","uuid":"f87f7a55-7aea-470b-8383-3d4ada475763","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:51:38.828Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6a65ebcb29b8f93","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
